{
  "title": "all_gather can change memory ordering of tensor",
  "issue_id": "163483",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nI try the `all_gather` operation on a tensor with `channels_last` format , then I found the memory ordering of output is changed so that the output and input are not aligned. This is not as expected. I think it's a BUG.\n\nThe reproducible minimal example, test.py is:\n```\nimport torch\n\ntorch.distributed.init_process_group(backend='nccl')\nrank = torch.distributed.get_rank()\nworld_size = torch.distributed.get_world_size()\ntorch.cuda.set_device(rank)\n\nx = torch.arange(0, 16).reshape(2, 2, 2, 2).cuda().to(memory_format=torch.channels_last)\nx_list = [torch.zeros_like(x) for _ in range(world_size)]\ntorch.distributed.all_gather(x_list, x)\n\nprint('rank_{}: {}\\n x:\\n{}\\n gathered_x:\\n{}\\n'.format(rank, torch.equal(x, x_list[rank]), x.storage(), x_list[rank].storage()))\n```\nThe command is:\n`torchrun --nproc_per_node 2 test.py`\nThe result is:\n```\nrank_1: False\n x:\n 0\n 4\n 1\n 5\n 2\n 6\n 3\n 7\n 8\n 12\n 9\n 13\n 10\n 14\n 11\n 15\n[torch.storage.TypedStorage(dtype=torch.int64, device=cuda:1) of size 16]\n gathered_x:\n 0\n 2\n 4\n 6\n 1\n 3\n 5\n 7\n 8\n 10\n 12\n 14\n 9\n 11\n 13\n 15\n[torch.storage.TypedStorage(dtype=torch.int64, device=cuda:1) of size 16]\nrank_0: False\n x:\n 0\n 4\n 1\n 5\n 2\n 6\n 3\n 7\n 8\n 12\n 9\n 13\n 10\n 14\n 11\n 15\n[torch.storage.TypedStorage(dtype=torch.int64, device=cuda:0) of size 16]\n gathered_x:\n 0\n 2\n 4\n 6\n 1\n 3\n 5\n 7\n 8\n 10\n 12\n 14\n 9\n 11\n 13\n 15\n[torch.storage.TypedStorage(dtype=torch.int64, device=cuda:0) of size 16]\n``` \n\n### Versions\ntorch==2.7.0a0+79aa17489c.nv25.4\nNVIDIA L40S\nDriver Version: 535.161.08\nCUDA Version: 12.9\n\ncc @ezyang @gchanan @zou3519 @kadeng @msaroufim @H-Huang @awgu @wanchaol @fegin @fduwjj @wz337 @wconstab @d4l3k @pragupta @dcci",
